[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0m[38;5;252m[1m## Summary of what was wrong and what was changed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two bugs were found in the C-to-Rust translation:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 1: Missing exported symbol [38;5;10mSPX_hash_message[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The test runner dynamically loads the shared library and looks up the symbol [38;5;10mSPX_hash_message[0m (the C code uses [38;5;10m#define hash_message SPX_NAMESPACE(hash_message)[0m which expands to [38;5;10mSPX_hash_message[0m). The Rust translation only had an internal [38;5;10mfn hash_message(...)[0m with no [38;5;10m#[no_mangle] pub extern "C"[0m export.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix[22m: Added a [38;5;10m#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern "C" fn SPX_hash_message(...)[0m wrapper that converts raw pointers to slices and delegates to the internal [38;5;10mhash_message[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 2: Incorrect bytes-to-bits conversion in [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m and [38;5;10mhash_message[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This was the subtle one. The BLAKE-256/512 [38;5;10mupdate[0m functions ([38;5;10mblake256_update[0m, [38;5;10mblake512_update[0m) take [38;5;10mdatalen[0m in [1mbits[22m, not bytes. The C wrapper functions [38;5;10mblake256()[0m and [38;5;10mblake512()[0m correctly multiply by 8 before calling [38;5;10mupdate[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
However, in [38;5;10mhash_blake.c[0m, the [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m and [38;5;10mhash_message[0m functions call [38;5;10mblakeX_update[0m [1mdirectly[22m (not through the wrapper), passing byte counts like [38;5;10mSPX_N[0m (32) without multiplying by 8. This means the C code passes 32 as a bit count, effectively hashing only 4 bytes of each input.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation "helpfully" added [38;5;10m* 8[0m to convert bytes to bits, which changes the semantics — it would hash all 32 bytes instead of just 4. While the C behavior looks like a quirk, it's the reference implementation's intended behavior, and the test vectors are generated from it.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix[22m: Removed the [38;5;10m* 8[0m multiplications from all six [38;5;10mblake512_update[0m calls in [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m (3 calls) and [38;5;10mhash_message[0m (3 calls), matching the C code's direct pass-through of byte counts.[0m[0m
